 "applies_to": "The EasyIO FD-20i: 10 analog (thermistor) inputs and 20 digital inputs, with per-input resistance, offset and temperature table objects.",
 "summary": "The FD-20i object list covers 10 analog inputs (AI 1-10) and 20 digital inputs (BI 1-20). For each analog input there is a read-only measured resistance (AV 1-10), a writable calibration offset (AV 11-20) and a writable temperature table number (AV 21-30) that picks the thermistor curve and degrees C or F.",
 "bacnet_transport": [],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Temperature table numbers (AV 21-30): 1 = NTC 10K Type 2 (°C), 2 = NTC 10K Type 2 with 11K shunt (°C), 3 = NTC 10K Type 3 (°C), 4 = NTC 10K Type 3 with 11K shunt (°C), 5 = NTC 20K (°C), 6-10 = the same sensors in °F. The default is 1.",
  "The guide also prints resistance-to-temperature tables for each sensor type; they are not object data and are left out.",
  "The object list does not state the BACnet transport or device instance.",
  "The list is published by EasyIO on the Johnson Controls documentation site."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "EasyIO FD-20i BACnet Objects",
